{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Usability Engineering.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Usability Engineering.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"usability engineering usability engineering","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Usability Engineering.md","fileName":"Usability Engineering.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Usability Engineering","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[UX Evaluation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["UX Evaluation","User Experience","Prototype","User Interface Evaluation","Usability","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Usability Engineering.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Usability Engineering.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"usability engineering usability engineering","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Usability Engineering.md","fileName":"Usability Engineering.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Usability Engineering","heading":"Usability Engineering","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Usability engineering is an iterative process for creating and refining a [[User Experience]]. A representative lifecycle moves through analysis, design, implementation, and evaluation, with iteration within and between stages.\n\nAnalysis identifies users, tasks, context, and requirements. Design turns those findings into interaction concepts. Implementation realizes concepts as [[Prototype]]s or working systems. [[User Interface Evaluation]] tests whether the design meets its goals and supplies evidence for revision.\n\nThe process can pursue [[Usability]], usefulness, and emotional impact. Iteration matters because guidelines and designer experience cannot predict every problem before people use the system.","tags":["baby"],"links":["UX Evaluation","User Experience","Pro